ause of more financial support from their snowboarding federation, had already won the parallel giant slalom a few days before. In that event Slovenian " [:a {:href "/athletes/119642"} "Žan Košir"] " had taken bronze, but he and Wild would meet in the final of this event."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Wild had made the final by defeating Austrian " [:a {:href "/athletes/119838"} "Benjamin Karl"] ", the 2009 and 2011 World Champion, in the semi-finals. Wild won the gold medal comfortably for his second gold medal in Sochi, while Karl easily won the bronze medal race over Italian " [:a {:href "/athletes/119551"} "Aaron March"] ". Two favorites went out in the 1/8th-final, as 2013 World Champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/119617"} "Rok Marguč"] " of Slovenia and Frenchman " [:a {:href "/athletes/119635"} "Sylvain Dufour"] ", the 2013/14 World Cup leader, failed to advance."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/128400"} "Vic Wild"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/RUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/RUS.png"}] "RUS"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "7"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/119642"} "Žan Košir"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SLO"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SLO.png"}] "SLO"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/119838"} "Benjamin Karl"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUT"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-fl